%N A401136 Square array read by antidiagonals downwards: T(n,k) = (Product_{j=1..n-1} prime(j))*prime(n)^k - 1 for n, k >= 1.
%C A401136 Row 1 consists of the Mersenne numbers 2^k - 1, and column 1 is A057588.
%C A401136 A400659(n) is the position of the first prime in row n.
%H A401136 Yagel Bar, <a href="/A401136/b401136.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..9870</a>.
%H A401136 Yagel Bar, <a href="https://yagelnumbers.org/paper/live/">Yagel Numbers: the Mersenne x Primorial Grid</a>.
%F A401136 T(n,k) = prime(n)*T(n,k-1) + prime(n) - 1 for k >= 2.
%e A401136 Array begins:
%e A401136   1, 3, 7, 15, 31, ...
%e A401136   5, 17, 53, 161, 485, ...
%e A401136   29, 149, 749, 3749, 18749, ...
%e A401136   209, 1469, 10289, 72029, 504209, ...
%e A401136   ...
%e A401136 For n = 4, the product of the first three primes is 30 and prime(4) = 7, so T(4,2) = 30*7^2 - 1 = 1469.
%e A401136 Read by antidiagonals downwards: 1; 3, 5; 7, 17, 29; 15, 53, 149, 209; ...
%o A401136 (PARI) T(n,k) = vecprod(primes(n-1))*prime(n)^k - 1
%o A401136 for(d=2,10,for(n=1,d-1,print1(T(n,d-n),", ")))
